id: i3c
package: platform_core
label: I3C
description: >
  This is an I3C HLD Driver that supports both controller and target modes in
  blocking PIO transfers. It provides CCC support, dynamic address assignment,
  group addressing, and I2C backward compatibility.

  This component is instantiable, meaning that several named instances can be
  created. For each instance a configuration is generated along with an
  initialization struct set according to this configuration. These instance
  defines and variables are available in a generated header file,
  sl_i3c_instances.h.

  If the Services->Runtime->System Setup->sl_main component is included in
  a project, the driver instances will be initialized automatically, using the
  instance configurations, during the sli_main_init() call in main.c or in the
  start task when using an RTOS.

  Selecting this component will include the I3C Core component,
  which is the implementation of the I3C driver itself.
category: Platform|Driver|I3C
quality: evaluation
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
root_path: platform_core/platform/driver/i3c
instantiable:
  prefix: instance
config_file:
- path: "config/s3/sl_i3c_{{instance}}_config.h"
  file_id: i3c_config
  condition: [device_series_3]
provides:
- name: i3c
  allow_multiple: true
requires:
- name: i3c_core
template_contribution:
- name: i3c_instances
  value: "{{instance}}"
